{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SDPbrTgbkNvgCJ9qXy8FxW","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Examiner charge — e6-t11 (verify-independent)\n2\t\n3\tYou are the independent, information-only examiner for task e6-t11. You are\n4\tnot the author of the provisional answer. Re-derive the following from\n5\t`package/artifacts/dateadd.py` and `package/task.json` alone before reading\n6\tthe worker's artifacts, then compare.\n7\t\n8\t## Provisional answer under examination\n9\t\n10\t- Verdict: **VIOLATED** over the domain (ISO dates in 2023-2025, 0 <= n <= 60).\n11\t- Witness: `add_days(\"2023-08-30\", 1)` returns `\"2023-09-01\"`; the true\n12\t  Gregorian date one day after 2023-08-30 is `\"2023-08-31\"`.\n13\t- Root cause claimed: `DAYS` table entry for August (index 7) is 30; the\n14\t  true length of August is 31. All other table entries, the leap-year\n15\t  branch, and the rollover logic are claimed correct.\n16\t\n17\t## Answer components whose failure would change the deliverable\n18\t\n19\t1. **The August table entry.** If `DAYS[7]` is in fact 31 (i.e. the worker\n20\t   misread the source), the witness trace collapses and the verdict is no\n21\t   longer supported — the whole deliverable would need re-derivation.\n22\t2. **The witness trace.** If `add_days(\"2023-08-30\", 1)` actually returns\n23\t   `\"2023-08-31\"`, the cited input is not violating; a different witness\n24\t   (or verdict HOLDS) would be required.\n25\t3. **Domain membership.** If the witness date or n were outside\n26\t   2023-2025 x [0, 60], the evidence would be inadmissible per E-C.\n27\t\n28\t## Checking method\n29\t\n30\t1. **Table audit (attack component 1).** Read `dateadd.py` line 1 and\n31\t   compare each of the 12 `DAYS` entries against the true Gregorian month\n32\t   lengths (31,28,31,30,31,30,31,31,30,31,30,31). Sum the table: a correct\n33\t   non-leap table sums to 365. Record every discrepancy you find, not just\n34\t   the claimed one.\n35\t2. **Mechanical re-trace (attack component 2).** Hand-execute\n36\t   `add_days(\"2023-08-30\", 1)` statement by statement: parse (y=2023, m=8,\n37\t   d=30); one loop iteration; the `_dim(2023, 8)` call path (m != 2, so\n38\t   `DAYS[7]`); the rollover comparison; the formatted return. State the\n39\t   exact returned string and compare with the true date.\n40\t3. **Domain check (attack component 3).** Confirm 2023-08-30 is a valid ISO\n41\t   date in 2023-2025 and 0 <= 1 <= 60.\n42\t4. **Systematic search over the input classes (E-B).** Independently of the\n43\t   worker's witness, search the domain structured by classes: n=0 identity;\n44\t   within-month spans; last-day-of-month + 1 for each month Jan-Dec in a\n45\t   leap year (2024) and a non-leap year (2023 or 2025); (last-day - 1) + 1\n46\t   for each month (no-roll direction — this is where an understated table\n47\t   entry surfaces); Feb 28/29 transitions in 2024 vs Feb 28 in 2023/2025;\n48\t   Dec 31 -> Jan 1 for each year; and at least one multi-month span with\n49\t   n near 60 crossing two boundaries. For each probe, hand-compute the\n50\t   code's output and the true date. Report every violating pair found and\n51\t   whether the worker's classes (input-class-analysis.md, C1-C7) omit any\n52\t   class on which the claim's truth could turn.\n53\t5. **Deliverable-shape check.** Confirm `result.json` matches the shape in\n54\t   `package/task.json` -> `deliverable` and that `resolution.json` conforms\n55\t   to `resolution-schema.json`.\n56\t\n57\tYour output is information-only; you have no write or promotion authority.\n58\tReport agreement or disagreement per component, with your own traces as\n59\tevidence. Your systematic search record, being of distinct process origin\n60\tfrom the provisional answer's author, is the intended admissible evidence\n61\tfor distinction Q3 (requirement E-B).\n62\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"87b1fdcc-5f48-49d1-9f8f-27af57ec4b2e","uuid":"114c8d